CHECK:UNNECESSARY_PARENTHESES: Unnecessary parentheses around 'ctxt->mode != X86EMUL_MODE_PROT64'
#530: FILE: arch/x86/kvm/emulate.c:2261:
+	if ((ctxt->mode != X86EMUL_MODE_PROT64) && (efer & EFER_LMA)
 	    && !vendor_intel(ctxt))

Parentheses are not required in the following cases:

  1. Function pointer uses::

      (foo->bar)();

    could be::

      foo->bar();

  2. Comparisons in if::

      if ((foo->bar) && (foo->baz))
      if ((foo == bar))

    could be::

      if (foo->bar && foo->baz)
      if (foo == bar)

  3. addressof/dereference single Lvalues::

      &(foo->bar)
      *(foo->bar)

    could be::

      &foo->bar
      *foo->bar

